# Test Scenarios for EV Charging Station API

## Quick Testing Guide

### 1. Test EV Owner Registration and Login
```bash
# Register new EV owner
POST /api/evownerauth/register
{
  "nic": "123456789V",
  "name": "Test User",
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "phone": "+94771234567",
  "password": "password123"
}

# Login EV owner
POST /api/evownerauth/login
{
  "nic": "123456789V",
  "password": "password123"
}
# Save the token from response for subsequent requests
```

### 2. Test Profile Access
```bash
# Get profile (requires EV owner token)
GET /api/evownerauth/profile
Authorization: Bearer {evowner_token}

# Update profile
PUT /api/evownerauth/profile
Authorization: Bearer {evowner_token}
{
  "nic": "123456789V",
  "name": "Updated Name",
  "email": "updated@example.com",
  "phone": "+94771234567",
  "isActive": true
}
```

### 3. Test System User Management
```bash
# Login as backoffice (create a user first via direct DB or existing admin)
POST /api/auth/login
{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "admin123"
}

# Create new system user (backoffice only)
POST /api/auth/register?username=operator1&password=operator123&role=StationOperator
Authorization: Bearer {backoffice_token}
```

### 4. Test Charging Station Management
```bash
# Create charging station (backoffice only)
POST /api/chargingstations
Authorization: Bearer {backoffice_token}
{
  "name": "Test Station",
  "address": "Colombo, Sri Lanka",
  "type": 0,  // AC = 0, DC = 1
  "availableSlots": 5,
  "schedule": "24/7",
  "isActive": true
}

# Get all active stations (public)
GET /api/chargingstations/active

# Update station (backoffice or operator)
PUT /api/chargingstations/{station_id}
Authorization: Bearer {operator_or_backoffice_token}
```

### 5. Test Booking Management
```bash
# Create booking (EV owner only)
POST /api/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {evowner_token}
{
  "chargingStationId": "{station_id}",
  "reservationDateTime": "2024-12-15T10:00:00Z"  // Within 7 days
}

# Get own bookings
GET /api/bookings/my-bookings
Authorization: Bearer {evowner_token}

# Update booking (EV owner, >12 hours before)
PUT /api/bookings/{booking_id}
Authorization: Bearer {evowner_token}
{
  "reservationDateTime": "2024-12-15T14:00:00Z"
}

# Cancel booking (EV owner, >12 hours before)
DELETE /api/bookings/{booking_id}
Authorization: Bearer {evowner_token}
```

### 6. Test Business Rules

#### Test 7-day Rule (Should Fail)
```bash
POST /api/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {evowner_token}
{
  "chargingStationId": "{station_id}",
  "reservationDateTime": "2024-12-25T10:00:00Z"  // More than 7 days
}
# Expected: 400 Bad Request
```

#### Test 12-hour Rule (Should Fail)
```bash
# Try to update/cancel booking with <12 hours remaining
PUT /api/bookings/{booking_id}
Authorization: Bearer {evowner_token}
{
  "reservationDateTime": "{time_within_12_hours}"
}
# Expected: 400 Bad Request
```

#### Test Station Deactivation with Active Bookings (Should Fail)
```bash
# Try to deactivate station with active bookings
DELETE /api/chargingstations/{station_id}
Authorization: Bearer {backoffice_token}
# Expected: 400 Bad Request if bookings exist
```

### 7. Test Authorization

#### Test EV Owner accessing other's booking (Should Fail)
```bash
# Try to update another user's booking
PUT /api/bookings/{other_user_booking_id}
Authorization: Bearer {evowner_token}
# Expected: 403 Forbidden
```

#### Test Station Operator creating stations (Should Fail)
```bash
POST /api/chargingstations
Authorization: Bearer {operator_token}
# Expected: 403 Forbidden (only backoffice can create)
```

